cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Smart Analysis: a Python pipeline engine for live adaptive microscopy"
message: "If you use this software in research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: de Hoog
    given-names: Thom
    affiliation: "Center for Microscopy and Image Analysis (ZMB), University of Zurich"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thomdehoog/smart-analysis"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - microscopy
  - image-analysis
  - bioimage-analysis
  - pipeline
  - cellpose
  - python
  - conda
  - live-acquisition
  - smart-microscopy
abstract: >-
  A Python pipeline engine for scientific image analysis workflows, with
  first-class support for live adaptive microscopy: streaming work
  tile-by-tile from an acquiring microscope, aggregating into regions, and
  feeding results back into acquisition decisions in real time. The same
  API also runs as a plain post-acquisition batch tool. Supports
  per-step conda environment isolation, scoped aggregation, priority
  scheduling, and warm-worker reuse for heavy resources like deep-learning
  models.
